---
Restore window drag and resize on Linux AppImage build.

The SDL2 main window in src/gui/gui.cpp:286 is created with
SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS. On Linux (X11/Wayland), borderless windows
have no native title bar to grab and no resize handles, so the
user cannot:
1. Drag-resize the window from any edge/corner
2. Drag the window around by its top bar

Maximize/minimize still work because those are bound to ImGui
toolbar buttons, not native chrome.

Two options:
A. Drop SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS — accept the OS-native title bar.
   Simplest fix, breaks the custom-chrome aesthetic.
B. Implement SDL_SetWindowHitTest to expose drag/resize regions
   on the custom title bar and window edges. Keeps the look.

Recommend B with a fallback to A if hit-testing proves flaky on
Wayland. Match GTK frontend behavior (which uses native chrome).

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Window can be dragged by clicking the top toolbar area
      (excluding interactive controls)
- [ ] Window can be resized by dragging any edge or corner
- [ ] Maximize/minimize buttons still function
- [ ] Cursor changes appropriately on resize edges
- [ ] Behavior tested on Linux (AppImage), Windows installer,
      and macOS .app
- [ ] Frontend parity preserved with GTK build

## Test Plan
- [ ] Drag window around screen on each platform
- [ ] Resize from each edge and corner
- [ ] Verify minimum window size still enforced (TASK-194)
- [ ] Verify no regression in toolbar button hover (TASK-146)
